<%# Auto-claim daemon setup — one paste-into-your-agent block: install the
    Go daemon, write its config with the token, run it as a login service.
    Locals: token, host, base_url, skill_url, fresh_token (true on the
    generating request — only then is the plaintext token real). %>
<% token_value = fresh_token ? token : "<regenerate your token in account settings — shown once>" %>
<% setup = <<~TEXT.strip
  Set up the Metis bridge daemon on this machine. It runs as a login service, auto-claims workflow steps marked Local, and works them with my own coding agent in per-task git worktrees.

  1. Install the daemon (one static Go binary):

  go install github.com/chagel/metis/clients/metis@latest
  # or from a checkout: cd clients/metis && go build -o /usr/local/bin/metis .

  2. Write ~/.metis/config.json (`metis init` scaffolds it) — the daemon only claims steps whose Metis project is mapped to a checkout here:

  {
    "agent": "claude",
    "servers": [
      {
        "name": "#{host}",
        "server": "#{base_url}",
        "token": "#{token_value}",
        "projects": { "<metis project name>": "~/path/to/its/checkout" }
      }
    ]
  }

  3. Install it as a login service and verify it polls:

  metis install
  tail -5 ~/.metis/daemon.log

  4. Optional: install the ops guide where you discover skills, for future troubleshooting:

  curl -fsSL --create-dirs #{skill_url} -o ~/.claude/skills/metis-bridge/SKILL.md
TEXT
%>
<%= render "settings/accounts/bridge_code_block", text: setup %>
